<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::maritime_transit_flow" target="global_monetary_stress::crossborder_capital" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained reductions in transit flow lower trade receipts and revenue visibility for trade-dependent economies, provoking portfolio reallocation and net capital outflows from those markets as investors de-risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::maritime_transit_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher, more reliable maritime transit throughput speeds delivery of servers, racks and heavy infrastructure to data‑center sites, enabling faster deployment schedules and a higher rate of compute capacity growth.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
