<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::insurance_premia_level" target="global_monetary_stress::bond_yield_levels" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid rise in insurance premia and war-risk surcharges raises perceived sovereign and corporate financing risk for countries and firms reliant on maritime trade, prompting investors to demand higher yields on sovereign and benchmark bonds.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::insurance_premia_level" target="russia_ukraine_energy::energy_price_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising war-risk and hull insurance premia raise marginal transport costs and increase delivery uncertainty, prompting abrupt rerouting, spot-market adjustments and hedging flows that amplify short-term energy-price swings.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::insurance_premia_level" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising war‑risk and transport insurance premia raise upfront and operating costs for building/operating data centers and fabs, eroding project returns and prompting investors to delay, scale back, or reallocate planned AI compute capital.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::insurance_premia_level" target="us_iran_confront::tanker_transit_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising war-risk and insurance premiums increase voyage costs and commercial risk for charterers, prompting rerouting, idling of tonnage, or refusal to enter contested chokepoints, thereby reducing tanker transits.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
