<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::military_response" target="russia_ukraine_energy::strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified naval/air patrols and interdiction operations around chokepoints constrain attackers' movement and logistics, reducing the frequency and severity of hostile strikes.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::military_response" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::geopolitical_tech_tensio" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid intensification of military operations around chokepoints provokes diplomatic recriminations, retaliatory measures, and accelerated export controls/sanctions tied to security concerns, directly heightening US–China technology and supply‑chain tensions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="maritime_chokepoints::military_response" target="us_iran_confront::military_tempo" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in military response intensity (escorts, interdictions, strikes) produces more operational actions and engagements in the region, directly raising the measured military operational tempo between U.S. and Iranian forces and proxies.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">maritime_chokepoints</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
