  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher fuel supply availability reduces headline energy inflation pressure and lowers near-term inflation risk, enabling central banks to adopt a less-tight (lower degree of tightening) monetary policy stance.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
