<edge source="russia_ukraine_energy::energy_price_volatility" target="global_monetary_stress::implied_policy_path" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising volatility in energy prices increases inflation uncertainty and risk premia, causing markets to reprice and imply a higher/earlier future policy-rate path to guard against upside inflation risk.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_energy::energy_price_volatility" target="maritime_chokepoints::insurance_premia_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger and more frequent swings in regional energy prices raise potential loss exposure for cargoes and owners, leading underwriters to widen war-risk and hull/cargo premia for vessels transiting high-risk chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
  <data key="d40">maritime_chokepoints</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_energy::energy_price_volatility" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_supply_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Large, rapid swings in regional energy prices raise operating costs and forced curtailments at energy‑intensive semiconductor fabs and memory production, degrading output reliability and tightening chip and memory availability for global supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_energy::energy_price_volatility" target="us_iran_confront::global_oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Larger and more frequent regional price swings increase risk premia and prompt precautionary buying and inventory draws, producing upward pressure and spikes in benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_energy</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_confront</data>
</edge>
